{
 "version": 1,
 "title": "Sync Scream",
 "category": "Leads and stabs",
 "text": "Sound: an aggressive, tearing lead for industrial and EBM: the tone rips upward at the start of each note, then settles into a hard, metallic buzz.\n\nHow it's built: two oscillators on the same note; the second is hard-synced to the first (SYNC), so its pitch is locked to the first and what changes is its tone. An envelope into the second's FM sweeps it up and back: that's the rip. Drive for edge, a filter to take the fizz off, a delay.\n\nPlay: single notes, in short phrases.\n\nTweak: the sweep envelope's DECAY, the second oscillator's FM (how far it sweeps) and TUNE, DRIVE.",
